        ":question/id": "570dc35b-e80f-5ece-8e6f-394d1b6948c7",
        ":question/problem": "$\\int (2\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+7\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C, \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (2\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+7\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x+7\\int \\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+7(-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)+C \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-7\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
